@startuml
' Slanted arrows (`->(n)` or `(n)<-`): each falls n pixels from its
' sender to its receiver, its heads turned along it; a bar that starts
' or ends with it does so where it arrives.
participant Client
participant Server
Client ->(20) Server ++ : request
Server -->(30) Client -- : response
Client (15)<- Server : notice
Client <->(20) Server : both ways
Client -> Server : level again
@enduml
